<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        Staff scheduling covers building the rota, handling shift changes and time off, and turning
        clock-ins into approved hours for payroll. Everything is under <strong>Rota</strong> in the
        Management menu.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="The pages">
        <ul>
            <li><a href="/manage/rota">Rota Builder</a>: plan shifts and publish them.</li>
            <li><a href="/manage/rota/timesheets">Timesheets</a>: check and approve clocked hours, and export them for payroll.</li>
            <li><a href="/manage/rota/requests">Shift Requests</a>: pick-ups, call-offs and swaps waiting for you.</li>
            <li><a href="/manage/rota/time-off">Time Off Requests</a>: approve time off, or record it for someone.</li>
            <li><a href="/manage/rota/time-off/types">Time Off Types</a>, <a href="/manage/rota/staff">Staff</a>,
                <a href="/manage/rota/positions">Positions</a> and <a href="/manage/rota/settings">Rota Settings</a>:
                set-up, covered on the <strong>Setting Up</strong> tab.</li>
            <li><a href="/manage/rota/terminals">Clock-In Terminals</a>: the tablets staff clock in on.</li>
        </ul>
        <FluentText>
            The Rota group in the menu shows a count when time-off or shift requests are waiting for you.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Locations">
        <FluentText>
            Rotas, requests and timesheets belong to a location. Managers work with the location they signed
            in to. Admins can switch between locations with the <strong>Location</strong> box at the top of
            each page. You can't approve your own requests or time; another manager or an admin has to.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="What staff see">
        <FluentText>
            Staff use <a href="/rota">My Shifts</a> to see their published shifts, ask to swap or drop a shift,
            pick up open shifts, request time off and set their availability. There's a separate staff guide,
            <a href="/help/my-shifts">My Shifts help</a>, you can point them to.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
